                "post_title": "Classic Italian Pasta Carbonara",
                "post_content": "<p>A traditional Roman pasta dish made with eggs, cheese, pancetta, and black pepper.</p><h3>Ingredients</h3><ul><li>400g spaghetti</li><li>200g pancetta or guanciale</li><li>4 large eggs</li><li>100g Pecorino Romano cheese</li><li>Black pepper to taste</li></ul><h3>Instructions</h3><ol><li>Cook pasta in salted boiling water until al dente.</li><li>While pasta cooks, fry pancetta until crispy.</li><li>Beat eggs with grated cheese and pepper.</li><li>Toss hot pasta with pancetta, then remove from heat.</li><li>Add egg mixture and toss quickly to coat.</li></ol>",
